> Explain the difference between RAM and storage in three sentences.
RAM is volatile memory that temporarily holds data and instructions the CPU needs for active tasks, offering fast access but losing its contents when power is removed. Storage (such as SSDs or HDDs) is non‑volatile, retaining data permanently even without power, though it is slower to read and write. Consequently, RAM provides short‑term working space, while storage holds the operating system, applications, and files for long‑term use.

